@page "/demo/patterns/credit-card-payment"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Credit card payment — Blazor Reference</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-page">

  <GupContentHeader PageTitle="Credit card payment">
    <PageSummary>Card entry — the field set, the order, and the grouping that keeps expiry and security code on one row.</PageSummary>
  </GupContentHeader>

  <div class="demo-body">

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">The pattern</h2>
      <DemoExample Id="the-pattern" File="CreditCardPayment.razor">
          <GupFormSection Heading="Payment details">
            <GupFormList>
              <GupInputField Name="name-on-card" Type="text">Name on card</GupInputField>

              <GupInputField Name="card-number" Type="text">
                <ChildContent>Card number</ChildContent>
                <Hint>The 16 digits on the front of the card.</Hint>
              </GupInputField>

              <GupTrack Gap="3" IsMultiline="true">
                <GupInputField Name="expiry-month" Type="text">
                  <ChildContent>Expiry month</ChildContent>
                  <Hint>MM</Hint>
                </GupInputField>
                <GupInputField Name="expiry-year" Type="text">
                  <ChildContent>Expiry year</ChildContent>
                  <Hint>YY</Hint>
                </GupInputField>
                <GupInputField Name="card-security-code" Type="text">
                  <ChildContent>Security code</ChildContent>
                  <Hint>3 digits on the back.</Hint>
                </GupInputField>
              </GupTrack>
            </GupFormList>
          </GupFormSection>
      </DemoExample>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Notes</h2>
      <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Expiry month, year and security code share a row via <a href="/demo/track">Track</a>, and wrap on a narrow screen rather than overflowing.</li>
        <li>GupInputField does not expose <code>autocomplete</code> or <code>inputmode</code> today, so the browser cannot autofill a card here — worth adding to the component before this pattern ships in a real service.</li>
        <li>Never log or echo the security code; it is entry-only.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>
